ApniRasoi Delivery Management

Data we need:
1. User base(total number of users(at mess customers, at home delivery customers, hybrid customers opting both)
2. Complications(lost packet of food,)
3. Pain points(A single customer with a fixed type of request(always asks for extra biryani on sunday))
4. EaseMyLiving bye bye!

Process Flow:
1. User registers on the site.
2. Opts for meal preference, pays for subscription.
3. User gets a QR that they can get scanned at mess to acquire food. (removes hassle of physical cards)
4. User chooses when they want home delivery and when they want to eat at the mess. (eg, Monday, Thursday, Friday eat at mess and other days home delivery)
5. Preference of people who chose home delivery for meal(s) is recorded.
6. Data is used to prepare MilkRun list.

MilkRun List:
A list of customers who chose home delivery for lunch or dinner or both on the specified dates.
AR can download daily list of customers who need home delivery twice.
    Daily list is in two kinds: lunch list and dinner list.
AR can know how many packets to prepare.
AR can deliver meals. (status updation is not required as everyone on list requires food delivery)


It contains following user columns:
1. Name + Veg/Non-Veg preference
2. No of days of subscription left
3. Address with landmark
4. Customization details if applicable

Problems solved:
1. Removed dependency on EaseMyLiving
2. Bringing organization in data to take effective actions.
3. Removed requirement of physical NFC cards.
4. Prevented double booking

Problems yet to solve:
1. Meal customization preferences are vague or too random to dispense.
2. Meal absenteeism(No lunch today) - Keeping track of this is difficult.
3. Paused mess for certian days

